From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 00:18:32 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: apple: t8132-j604: keep the SIO off until
 its power domain is qualified

The SIO's mailbox and DMA controller sit in the SIO_CPU power domain,
which this board leaves disabled (t8132-j604-pmgr.dtsi: no qualified
power sequence). Commit 075f6f3764db ("arm64: dts: apple: t8132-j604:
hand the SIO to the boot loader") enabled the mailbox and the DART and
added the "sio" alias, through which the boot loader enables the DMA
controller, but left SIO_CPU disabled.

With the domain disabled, no power domain device exists, so the mailbox
gets no device link to it. It probes, waits for its supplier until the
deferred probe timeout, then fails with -110 because the SIO never
answers; the DMA controller stays deferred on the mailbox.

Undo the enable: drop the alias and the mailbox and DART status
overrides, so the SIO, its mailbox and its DART stay disabled together
with SIO_CPU, as before that commit. DPA1, the only SIO client on this
board, was already disabled. The SIO, its domain and DPA1 can be
enabled together once the SIO is qualified.

Fixes: 075f6f3764db ("arm64: dts: apple: t8132-j604: hand the SIO to the boot loader")
Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5.5
(cherry picked from commit 52a84b0bddd55b7281749a02b73cb41c6851e927)
---
 .../arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132-j604-hdmi.dtsi | 22 ++++++++-----------
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+), 13 deletions(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132-j604-hdmi.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132-j604-hdmi.dtsi
index f402aff336..e5451ee8c3 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132-j604-hdmi.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132-j604-hdmi.dtsi
@@ -34,11 +34,18 @@
  * powered down.
  *
  * The port's audio is DPA1 (ADT dp-audio1, SIO channel 0x66, power gate DPA1,
- * the dp-audio node dcpext0 names), as on the M3 Pro HDMI port. The SIO
- * that carries it is enabled by the boot loader (alias below). DPA1 stays
+ * the dp-audio node dcpext0 names), as on the M3 Pro HDMI port. DPA1 stays
  * disabled until the adopted dcpext session serves audio: the dcpext is no
  * component of the DRM device, so no audio component could bind to it yet.
  *
+ * The SIO that carries it (t8132-sio.dtsi) stays off as well, with its
+ * mailbox and DART, and the board gives it no "sio" alias, so the boot loader
+ * does not enable it either. Its mailbox and DMA controller are in the SIO_CPU
+ * power domain, which stays disabled on this board (t8132-j604-pmgr.dtsi:
+ * no qualified power sequence). Enabling them without it leaves the mailbox
+ * waiting for a domain that is never registered and the SIO never answering.
+ * SIO, its domain and DPA1 are enabled together once SIO is qualified.
+ *
  * Copyright The Asahi Linux Contributors
  */
 
@@ -46,20 +53,9 @@
 	aliases {
 		/* m1n1 copies the ATC tunables through this alias. */
 		atcphy2 = &atcphy2;
-		/* The boot loader builds the SIO's tables and enables it by this alias. */
-		sio = &sio;
 	};
 };
 
-/* The SIO's mailbox and DART; the boot loader enables the SIO with its firmware. */
-&sio_mbox {
-	status = "okay";
-};
-
-&dart_sio0 {
-	status = "okay";
-};
-
 /*
  * The SoC node describes ATC2 with its USB windows and is named after the
  * first of them. No USB controller uses ATC2 on this board: describe it again
